<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Template only. A person installs this in slice S5, on the lease host, as an
  agent of the dedicated `seat` user (outside group staff), after pinning the
  Ollama digest in models.lock. Nothing in this repo loads, bootstraps or
  enables it. The paths below are placeholders for that user.

  Why each key (runtimes-and-host.md 3.1):
  - RunAtLoad false: a reboot or a fresh bootstrap never fires a beat before
    HALT and Keychain state are settled. KeepAlive stays unset, since it
    implies RunAtLoad.
  - StartInterval 1800: launchd never overlaps two runs of this job, and a
    tick slept through is missed, not owed. The mkdir lock still guards
    manual and kickstart runs.
  - Absolute paths everywhere: launchd's PATH is /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin.
  - The config is the operator's, beside HALT in /Users/Shared/kingdom-seat/
    (owner the operator, mode 0644): the tick refuses a config the seat user
    owns or could replace, since the config names the HALT file.
  - Umask 63 (octal 077): logs and state are private to the seat user.
    status.json is the one exception: the seat writes it 0644 on purpose,
    because REGISTRY reads it.
  - AbandonProcessGroup unset: when the job dies, launchd kills the tick's
    own process group. The seat child is not in it: it leads its own group
    so the watcher can signal it whole. The watcher forwards launchd's
    SIGTERM to that group (TERM, then KILL after term_grace_s), so a stopped
    job stops its seat too; ExitTimeOut must stay above term_grace_s.
  - The tick runs with no secret in its environment; the signer reads
    Keychain through /usr/bin/security, and nothing is sourced from a home.
    Because /usr/bin/security is the process that asks, the items are ACL'd
    to it, and any process running as the seat user can read them: the seat
    user's account is the custody boundary, so nothing else runs as it.
  - ProgramArguments run bun on the source for now. A compiled, stably signed
    binary would not by itself narrow who can read the keys while reads go
    through /usr/bin/security; that needs a signer that reads through the
    Security framework itself (see src/signer/keychain.ts).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>dev.kingdom.citizen-seat</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/seat/.bun/bin/bun</string>
    <string>/Users/seat/kingdom-seat/src/cli.ts</string>
    <string>tick</string>
    <string>--config</string>
    <string>/Users/Shared/kingdom-seat/config.json</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/seat/Library/Application Support/kingdom-seat</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>Umask</key><integer>63</integer>
  <key>ExitTimeOut</key><integer>20</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/seat/Library/Logs/kingdom-seat/tick.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/seat/Library/Logs/kingdom-seat/tick.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
